{"description":"We are a group of individuals who are looking to push our skills","image":"https://assets.spaceappschallenge.org/media/images/Dapper_Chimp_in_a_Black_Suit.2e16d0ba.fill-300x250.png","summary":"NASA has spent twenty years burning things in microgravity, and the results sit in the PSI archive as 24 experiments in 21 different spreadsheets. We put every row (1,993) into one database and built a console that ranks that evidence against a fire-safety question.\n\nPick a material, concern, airflow, oxygen and gravity, or just type the question: an open six-criterion rubric (fuel, concern, airflow, oxygen, scale, data) scores all 24 investigations 0-100, shows the facts behind each score and explains the top three. The same question goes to Claude, which may only run read-only SQL on that database; the SQL it ran is shown and the investigations it cites light up in the ranking.\n\nHeadline finding: no cabin material has been burned above 22.2% oxygen in microgravity, and nothing has burned at Moon or Mars gravity, so Moon-base air (26.5-34% O2) is covered only by gas-burner and fuel-drop tests.\n\nLive console with the AI: https://gilbert-reward-sin-sold.trycloudflare.com\nStatic copy: https://claude.ai/artifact/SXXfkftkqTpnePDE8ZeUqE","details":"<p>undefined</p>","dataRefs":[["PSI-25 - BASS-II","https://psi.nasa.gov/physci/repo/data/investigations/PSI-25"],["PSI-159 - ACME CFI-G","https://psi.nasa.gov/physci/repo/data/investigations/PSI-159"],["PSI-98 - SAFFIRE-I","https://psi.nasa.gov/physci/repo/data/investigations/PSI-98"],["PSI-102 - SAME","https://psi.nasa.gov/physci/repo/data/investigations/PSI-102"],["PSI-99 - SAFFIRE-II","https://psi.nasa.gov/physci/repo/data/investigations/PSI-99"],["PSI-26 - BASS","https://psi.nasa.gov/physci/repo/data/investigations/PSI-26"],["PSI-100 - SAFFIRE-III","https://psi.nasa.gov/physci/repo/data/investigations/PSI-100"],["PSI-20 - ACME BRE","https://psi.nasa.gov/physci/repo/data/investigations/PSI-20"],["PSI-69 - FLEX",